              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for ululation, then the Bengali for the groom's wedding party."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: রাজ্য",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "রাজ্য — rājyô — \"a kingdom; a state\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "অনেক দিন আগে এখানে একটা ছোট রাজ্য ছিল। ônek din āge ekhāne ekṭā chhoṭo rājyô chhilô. Long ago there was a small kingdom here."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "রাজ্য (rājyô) is Sanskrit rājya, 'kingship, sovereignty; a kingdom' (Monier-Williams), the abstract of rājan, a king — রাজা. Today it is also a state of India."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
